<title>USA: Carolina Power shuts Harris N.C. nuke.</title>
<headline>Carolina Power shuts Harris N.C. nuke.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carolina Power and Light Co's 880 megawatt Harris nuclear unit was shut Sunday for repairs, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said in Monday's plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in New Hill, N.C., was in hot shutdown mode while operators made repairs to the generator exciter, the NRC report also stated.</p>
<p>A tentative restart date of July 24 was given by the NRC.</p>
<p>((--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
